  "loc": "Introduction, p.3; Section II Model, p.8",
  "quote": "an interest group such as a firm mobilizes voters",
  "note": "The main object is a signalling game in which an interest group mobilizes voters to influence a single politician's policy choice. The policy is chosen by one decision-maker, not aggregated from several agents' inputs by a voting rule. The election appears only as a stage that drives the politician's objective (maximizing votes); no electoral rule or its strategic or computational aspects is studied. Coding stopped per C0."
